Phase 14 compatibility audit follow-up — 2026-10-12 UTC

- Re-audited the public `TransactionMQProducer` API against the pinned Java 5.5.1 source. Added a Rust `new_with_rpc_hook` path through `Producer` into `ClientRuntimeManager::get_or_create_with_hook`, re-exported `RpcHook`, documented the constructor/config mapping, and matched Java deprecation metadata for legacy listener and pool setters. Added public-crate and runtime-registration tests.
- Compared custom `ExecutorService.submit` behavior with the Rust dispatcher. The previous dispatcher awaited each submitted callback, serializing otherwise parallel custom executors. It now submits checks independently, tracks completion work for bounded shutdown, and caps accepted custom-executor work. Added a blocking two-check concurrency regression test.
- Final strict workspace tests caught no product failures. During test authoring, typed `Arc::ptr_eq` assertions initially needed coercion to trait-object `Arc`s; corrected and reran the suites successfully.
- `cargo test --workspace --locked` — PASS on final implementation; `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-producer --locked` — PASS (57 unit, 3 producer, 5 scripted-send, 6 transaction tests); `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings` — PASS; `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` — PASS; `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --test headers --locked` — PASS (11 tests); `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test` — PASS.
- A final `mvn -o -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` first exposed nondeterministic field ordering from Java `Map.of` in `TransactionFixtures`. Parsed fixture values were identical; exact-string drift came from randomized map iteration. Replaced it with `TreeMap`, regenerated twice with identical SHA-256 `cfa19e98ad567b42a4e462c11906e6e49589e59557817d7359e990d9b4c314e5`, then reran Maven verify — PASS.
